# Directory-level context for packages/warpline/src/fabric — the canonical
# component docs live in packages/warpline/.purpose (#strand #fabric #fabric-dag
# #fabric-refs #seal #pick #admit #resolve #grade #fabric-verify #fabric-repair
# #anchor #backfill #restore #fabric-lock #hook #scratch #materialize
# #warpline-config #shadow-gate #native-write-path #stake #stake-journal).
name: fabric
description: >-
  The Warpline fabric — the native, git-independent WRITE layer: the append-only
  PICK-DAG ledger (.warpline/fabric.jsonl), strand identity across three schema
  epochs (pick:v0 self-hash → pick:v2 linear chain → pick:v3 position-free DAG
  identity, docs/specs/warpline-v3-identity.md), the derived DAG index (dag.ts),
  pickId refs with per-ref CAS (refs.ts), seal/pick/admit/resolve write paths,
  calibration grading, epoch anchoring, verify, git-absent restore, the R1
  shadow gate (config.ts/shadow.ts — observe-only admit verdicts), and the
  phase-0 native write path (native.ts — fork/propose/admit/resolve, no git).
context:
  - "v3 identity (V3.1): pickId = H(parents + content); NO ledger position; buildStrandV3 is the only v3 constructor; sealed v3 bytes are final"
  - "refs (V3.2): refs/heads/<name> hold pickIds; migrateSelvageToRefs is the ONE-TIME founder-visible migration — never automatic"
  - "coexistence invariant: this layer writes ONLY under .warpline/, never the user's git HEAD/index/worktree"
  - "durability (C-7): every ledger append, tip-pointer publish and scratch-ref write goes through ../warp/durable.ts (#warp-durable) — fsync the staging file, rename, fsync the parent dir. Never hand-roll writeFileSync(tmp)+rename here again"
  - "staging names (C-15): `<target>.tmp.<pid>.<n>` via tmpNameFor. A shared `${p}.tmp` defeats the per-ref CAS, which runs BEFORE the write; and refs/heads residue must never be readable as a ref (isRefName = REF_NAME ∧ no `..` ∧ !isTmpResidue, enforced on BOTH listRefs and writeRef)"
  - "native-first R1 (shadow.ts): shadow admits are observe-only — the ONLY write is one row in .warpline/shadow/verdicts.jsonl; opt-in via .warpline/config.json shadowGate"
  - "native-first phase 0 (native.ts): propose seals v3 SCRATCH strands; admit weaves via materializeMergedStateNative only; the git-era seal path stays v2 until the founder-visible cutover"
  - "truncation evidence (C-6): the hash chain only proves the strands PRESENT agree; stake-journal.ts is the only thing attesting how many there should be. It is advisory IN (absent/unreadable/disabled ⇒ no evidence, never a failure) and hard OUT (a COMPLETED checkpoint naming a missing strand ⇒ stake-journal-orphan, exit 1). Never make the reader throw"
  - "repair (C-13): fsync makes an append DURABLE, not ATOMIC — a torn tail line is still reachable. scanFabric is the tolerant read UNDER the fail-closed readFabric; repair.ts truncates TAIL tears only, dry-run by default, quarantining the original first and republishing a raw Buffer PREFIX (never re-serialized — pickIds and the anchor prefix digest hash the stored bytes)"
components:
  fabric:
    description: >-
      See the #fabric component (and siblings) in packages/warpline/.purpose for
      the full per-module documentation.
    tags: [warpline, fabric, v3]
